ze 1.0 1.0)) hide)) (instances (project "machine_permission" (path "/d1225b76-a480-512d-b5fe-41abcd9cddf7" (reference "#FLG2") (unit 1))))) (wire (pts (xy 317.5 556.26) (xy 317.5 561.34)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "03489873-82e7-5731-9aed-2d35dd397e94")) (label "LOGIC_GND" (at 317.5 561.34 0) (effects (font (size 0.95 0.95)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1fae90fa-22c4-5ca5-bb39-97f96a8d499e")) (text "INDEPENDENT WATCHDOG AND EDGE-ARMED GLOBAL PERMISSION - ENGINEERING CANDIDATE" (at 20.32 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2)) (justify left top)) (uuid "732f72f0-767a-5add-8b00-cadf2f75d266")) (text "Seven ICs; no firmware timer owns the external watchdog. IO_3V3=3.2-3.4V, common LOGIC_GND. Eight motors minimum / twelve expansion requirement." (at 20.32 27.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7b7661ef-3fde-5e2b-8eb8-34867ac8aedc")) (text "1. Always-enabled watchdog; WDO + ENOUT wired together" (at 20.32 48.26 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d7987a24-72b2-516e-8c91-1a2d2d64ac80")) (text "2. Schmitt inputs for open-drain watchdog and CDONE" (at 264.16 48.26 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "84920c1b-5478-5050-b7e5-3a5032a39f2c")) (text "3. Rail-to-rail WDI buffer; FALLING edges feed timer" (at 477.52 48.26 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4c5904fe-b344-576a-9968-7def9c1f1b78")) (text "4. Raw interlock" (at 20.32 246.38 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7c27ceb4-bd5d-576f-8c3b-cda440af0f24")) (text "5. Raw return and latch clear" (at 264.16 246.38 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4e1cef66-4502-5f51-8e73-51cce7009551")) (text "6. Accepted ARM edge; async clear" (at 477.52 246.38 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e346ea86-ed06-5880-86f4-70d520787e32")) (text "7. Final physical permit" (at 685.8 246.38 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ba4f6384-58db-59d6-83c8-cd9fe1058728")) (text "120pF:64.288ms nominal watchdog. NOT20ms.\n100pF nominal would violate tested minimum at -tolerance.\nFalling progress edge occurs every TWO accepted UPDATEs.\nWDO auto-releases after170-230ms; heartbeat alone\ncannot set the arm latch. SYNC + deliberate ARM required.\nCDONE pullup belongs to FPGA block: no local pulldown." (at 695.96 60.96 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left top)) (uuid "da2647e3-543b-50e7-bdb0-effaa8853ef8")) (text "HW_WATCHDOG_OK_N -> RTL inhibit_n. Never return TX_PERMIT there.\nRaw interlock has no endpoint_ready / motion_request / latch dependency.\nD is permanently HIGH; clock is FPGA_MOTION_REQUEST rising edge.\nAsynchronous clear is raw interlock AND endpoint_ready.\nTX_PERMIT = latched_arm AND motion_request AND raw_interlock." (at 477.52 462.28 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c47e3738-cfc8-57fd-b23b-8140c805abff")) (text "TX_PERMIT drives six AM26C31 G inputs + six10k pulldowns; /G fixedHIGH.\nDefaultLOW disables transmitters. Per-drive active-low enables are separate.\nEXT_PERMIT_3V3 is protected internal logic, never raw24V or certified E-stop.\nSingle-channel candidate: no safety certification, fault tolerance or controlled stop.\nBrownout slew, partial power, metastability, wiring and physical timing remain open.\nClearing output permission can truncate a pulse; reconcile position before recovery." (at 477.52 500.38 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b8267920-cbfb-589d-aca3-9c419352ed9e")))
